<h3>Spelling the Major Scale by Whole/Half Steps</h3>
<p>To make sure you know how to form the scale, I provided a step-by-step.<=
/p>
<ol>
<li>Start with the root note for the key you are using. In the key of F, yo=
ur root is F.</li>
<li>Follow the interval formula for a major scale (W-W-H-W-W-W-H).
<ol>
<li>A whole step up from F is G.</li>
<li>A whole step up from G is A.</li>
<li>A half step up from A is Bb. To maintain a half step, we must use accid=
entals. &nbsp;In this case it is a flat.</li>
<li>A whole step up from Bb is C.</li>
<li>A whole step up from C is D.</li>
<li>A whole step up from D is E.</li>
<li>A half step up from E is F. E to F is naturally a half step.</li>
</ol>
</li>
</ol>
